Glossary of Core Terms

Term	Definition
Autogeneration	The principle of self-maintenance of informational curvature within a cohesive medium; a non-Markovian process where continuation is determined by the integrated history of a system's trajectory.
Autogenerative System	A formal mathematical structure, defined as a tuple (X, F, \Phi, \mu, \nabla), that integrates a statistical manifold (Fisher geometry), a sheaf of continuations, a non-Markovian flow, a path-space measure with polynomial tails, and a compositional connection.
Cohesive ∞-Topos	A higher-categorical framework that unifies discrete, continuous, and topological structures. It serves as the universal space for modeling autogenerative systems, equipped with adjoint modalities (Shape, Flat, Sharp) for translating between these domains.
Transjective Endofunctor	A composite functor, T = G \circ F, that models the reciprocal loop between two categories, such as a semantic space (\mathcal{C}_1) and an embodied motor space (\mathcal{C}_2). It represents the cycle of intention-enactment-assimilation.
Idempotent Closure	The equilibrium state of a transjective endofunctor, where T \circ T \simeq T. This condition signifies perfect automation or comprehension, where the cognitive loop has stabilized and produces no further change.
Aspect Relegation Theory (ART)	The theory that cognitive automation is a process of "relegating" conscious, high-effort processes to automatic, low-energy sub-systems, formalized as the achievement of idempotent closure and the flattening of relevance fields.
Relevance-Resonance Functional (L)	A joint energy functional defined as \mathcal{L}[x] = |\nabla R(x)|^2 + D_{\mathrm{FR}}(\nabla F^{*} g_2, g_1), where D_{\mathrm{FR}} is the Fisher-Rao divergence. Its minimization drives the system toward aspect relegation and transjective closure.
Recursive Semantic Vector Plenum (RSVP)	A dynamical system comprising a scalar potential field (\Phi), a vector flow field (\mathbf{v}), and an entropy field (S). It provides a physical and field-theoretic interpretation of the autogenerative statistical manifold.
Amplitwistor Manifold	An oscillatory phase space that models the interactions of cortical columns using complex spinor amplitudes, providing a neurodynamic substrate for the implementation of cognitive functors.
Barenholtz Consistency Principle	The principle stating the equivalence of three conditions for understanding: cohomological flatness (global coherence), energetic smoothness (thermodynamic equilibrium), and informational persistence (non-Markovian memory).


