dark markdown-new-styling"><p data-start="0" data-end="119">Here’s a <strong data-start="9" data-end="34">complete <code data-start="20" data-end="32">index.html</code></strong> for your repository — a self-contained retro-green, terminal-style interface that:</p>
<ul data-start="121" data-end="477">
<li data-start="121" data-end="230">
<p data-start="123" data-end="230">Lists and opens Markdown blog articles from the <code data-start="171" data-end="184">background/</code> folder <em data-start="192" data-end="200">inline</em> (without leaving the page).</p>
</li>
<li data-start="231" data-end="322">
<p data-start="233" data-end="322">Includes a <strong data-start="244" data-end="271">monochrome audio player</strong> for your <code data-start="281" data-end="319">Geometric_Consciousness_and_LLMs.mp3</code>.</p>
</li>
<li data-start="323" data-end="405">
<p data-start="325" data-end="405">Displays <strong data-start="334" data-end="354">synced subtitles</strong> from your <code data-start="365" data-end="371">.vtt</code> file directly under the player.</p>
</li>
<li data-start="406" data-end="477">
<p data-start="408" data-end="477">Provides an <strong data-start="420" data-end="444">Escape / Back button</strong> to return to the article list.</p>
</li>
</ul>
<p data-start="479" data-end="639">You can place this <code data-start="498" data-end="510">index.html</code> in your repository root. It will work as a static file on GitHub Pages or locally in any browser (with appropriate permissions).</p>
