down prose dark:prose-invert w-full break-words dark markdown-new-styling"><p data-start="0" data-end="208">Excellent — glad the retro interface worked! The subtitle issue is likely just a small parsing or file-path mismatch. Let’s fix that cleanly and robustly so your <code data-start="162" data-end="168">.vtt</code> subtitles sync properly with the audio.</p>
<hr data-start="210" data-end="213">
<h3 data-start="215" data-end="274">✅ Here’s an improved version of the <strong data-start="255" data-end="274">subtitle system</strong></h3>
<p data-start="275" data-end="397">Drop this updated JavaScript block (replace the <code data-start="323" data-end="333">&lt;script&gt;</code> section that handles subtitles) into your current <code data-start="384" data-end="396">index.html</code>.</p>
<p data-start="399" data-end="407">It adds:</p>
<ul data-start="408" data-end="697">
<li data-start="408" data-end="458">
<p data-start="410" data-end="458">Automatic detection of both <code data-start="438" data-end="444">.vtt</code> and <code data-start="449" data-end="455">.srt</code>.</p>
</li>
<li data-start="459" data-end="557">
<p data-start="461" data-end="557">Correct parsing of WebVTT time formats (<code data-start="501" data-end="512">00:00.000</code> → <code data-start="515" data-end="524">seconds</code>) <strong data-start="526" data-end="533">and</strong> SRT (<code data-start="539" data-end="553">00:00:00,000</code>).</p>
</li>
<li data-start="558" data-end="652">
<p data-start="560" data-end="652">Continuous syncing using a binary search rather than a full scan for smoother performance.</p>
</li>
<li data-start="653" data-end="697">
<p data-start="655" data-end="697">A visible “Subtitles loaded” confirmation.</p>
</li>
</ul>
