 6.01057 5.53708 6.00551 6.00391 6.00391C6.00551 5.53708 6.01057 5.14051 6.03809 4.80371C6.0755 4.34588 6.15483 3.94012 6.34668 3.56348L6.46875 3.34473C6.77282 2.84912 7.20856 2.44514 7.72949 2.17969L7.87207 2.11328C8.20855 1.96886 8.56979 1.90385 8.9707 1.87109C9.42091 1.83432 9.978 1.83496 10.667 1.83496H13.5C14.1891 1.83496 14.746 1.83431 15.1963 1.87109C15.6541 1.90851 16.0599 1.98788 16.4365 2.17969L16.6553 2.30176C17.151 2.60585 17.5548 3.04244 17.8203 3.56348L17.8867 3.70606C18.031 4.04235 18.0962 4.40306 18.1289 4.80371C18.1657 5.25395 18.165 5.81091 18.165 6.5V9.33301Z"></path></svg>Copy code</button></div></div></div><div class="overflow-y-auto p-4" dir="ltr"><code class="whitespace-pre! language-markdown"><span><span><span class="hljs-section"># The Landscape of Thought  </span></span><span>
</span><span><span class="hljs-section">## How Your Mind Makes Efficient Choices</span></span><span>

---

</span><span><span class="hljs-section">## Introduction — The Art of a Single Thought</span></span><span>

Deciding what to eat for lunch feels simple. Under the surface, your brain simulates futures, retrieves memories, weighs tradeoffs, predicts satisfaction, prices effort against reward, and collapses millions of possible futures into </span><span><span class="hljs-emphasis">*one*</span></span><span>.  

This is not magic. It is </span><span><span class="hljs-strong">**physics**</span></span><span>.

This article explains the claim that </span><span><span class="hljs-strong">**all thinking is sparse policy selection**</span></span><span> — a process through which the mind navigates a </span><span><span class="hljs-strong">**physical landscape of possibility**</span></span><span>, eliminating almost all options, and selecting one coherent plan.

---

</span><span><span class="hljs-section">## 1. The Latent Action Space — A Map of Possible Minds</span></span><span>

Thinking occurs in a </span><span><span class="hljs-strong">**latent action space**</span></span><span> — a vast plenum of possible actions, memories, concepts, and futures.

This landscape is shaped by three interacting fields:

| Field | Meaning | Intuition |
|---|---|---|
| </span><span><span class="hljs-strong">**Visibility Potential (Φ)**</span></span><span> | Value / salience / "what matters" | The hills and valleys of significance |
| </span><span><span class="hljs-strong">**Agency Flow (v)**</span></span><span> | Paths of possible action | The current you move along |
| </span><span><span class="hljs-strong">**Entropy (S)**</span></span><span> | Uncertainty / confusion | The fog hiding parts of the map |

Thinking = navigating this landscape to a </span><span><span class="hljs-strong">**low entropy**</span></span><span>, </span><span><span class="hljs-strong">**high relevance**</span></span><span>, </span><span><span class="hljs-strong">**high agency**</span></span><span> region.

---

</span><span><span class="hljs-section">## 2. Policies — Paths Through Thought</span></span><span>

A </span><span><span class="hljs-strong">**policy**</span></span><span> is a planned route through this internal world.

Two kinds:

| Type | Description | Examples |
|---|---|---|
| </span><span><span class="hljs-strong">**Internal Policies**</span></span><span> | Never executed externally. Used for imagination, planning, reasoning | simulating a conversation, recalling a memory |
| </span><span><span class="hljs-strong">**External Policies**</span></span><span> | Become real-world actions | speaking, typing, moving your body |

Your brain must choose </span><span><span class="hljs-emphasis">*one path*</span></span><span> from astronomical possibilities.

---

</span><span><span class="hljs-section">## 3. The Core Engine — Minimizing Surprise</span></span><span>

The brain is a </span><span><span class="hljs-strong">**prediction machine**</span></span><span>.

It chooses policies to </span><span><span class="hljs-strong">**minimize free energy**</span></span><span>—the mismatch between:

</span></span></code></div></div></pre>
<p data-start="2146" data-end="2229">What it expects to happen<br data-start="2171" data-end="2174">
