Sparsity Law	Policy activation is sublinear (‖π‖₀ ∼ n^α, α &lt; 1).	Activation scales linearly (α ≈ 1).
Entropy Bound	Semantic entropy growth in knowledge systems is linear (S(t) ≤ S₀ + κΛt).	Growth is superlinear (S(t) ∼ t^(1+δ)).
Lightcone Constraint	Semantic influence propagates at a finite speed (d ≤ cst).	Influence spreads instantaneously.
Criticality	A sharp phase transition exists for semantic coherence vs. sparsity pressure (ξ ∼ |Λ− Λc|⁻ν).	Coherence decays smoothly with no threshold.
Memory Decay	Unreinforced information decays exponentially (H(t) ∼ e⁻εt).	Retention follows a power-law.
Invariant Alignment	Under self-improvement, an objective invariant I remains constant (∆I_t = 0).	The invariant drifts (∆I_t &gt; ε).
Scalar Extraction	In extractive platforms, effective coherence/visibility (C_effective) decreases as extraction pressure increases.	C_effective is independent of extraction.

Proposed experimental protocols include neural sparsity scaling in brains and models, entropy auditing of Wikipedia, influence radius tests on social media, and critical sparsity sweeps in transformers.

6. Key Quotes and Terminology

6.1. Defining Quotes

* On the goal of intelligence: "Intelligent agents... must capture this structure of the world... the internal representations of their minds and their brains must capture the structure of the world."
* On the failure of SGD: "Conventional SGD in deep learning finds neural representations which are actually fractured and entangled... It looks like a complete mess, right? It looks like complete spaghetti."
* On sparse cognition: "Cognition is not search over all policies, but compressed survival of a sparse basis of viable flows."
* On platform extraction: "This corresponds to the phenomenology of 'work harder, reach less'."
* On the nature of thought: "To think is to pay an entropy cost to sculpt a local region of the plenum using a sparse superposition of admissible field deformations."
* On true alignment: "How do we ensure that misaligned goals are not representable inside the system, even in principle...? A system is safely alignable if and only if misalignment is an unrepresentable state."
* On the self: "The RSVP mind: not a ghost in the machine, but a persistent, conscious distortion in the fabric of entropy and flow."

6.2. Glossary of Key Terms

Term	Definition
EBSSC	Entropy-Bounded Sparse Semantic Calculus: The core computational framework modeling cognition.
RSVP	Relativistic Scalar–Vector Plenum: The physical, field-theoretic substrate for EBSSC.
Plenum	The space where cognition occurs, comprising the Φ, v, and S fields.
Semantic Sphere	A bounded, multimodal, typed representation of a concept with internal entropy and provenance.
SpherePOP	A calculus of primitive operators (pop, merge, collapse) that act on Semantic Spheres.
Φ (Phi)	Scalar Potential Field: Represents semantic density, visibility, or pragmatic value.
v	Vector Flow Field: Represents agency, policy application, or intentional action.
S	Entropy Field: Represents uncertainty, disorder, or informational dispersion.
Sparse Policy Selection	The core cognitive process of choosing latent actions by minimizing a free-energy objective with an L1 penalty.
Invariant Alignment	An AI alignment paradigm focused on making a system's core objectives an invariant (fixed point) under optimization.
Scalar Extraction	A field-theoretic model of extractive platforms where user agency (v) is opposed by visibility potential (Φ).
Texture/Time Crystals	A proposed dual-currency system for non-extractive platforms that rewards structural coherence and persistent influence.</div></div></div></div></div><div class="z-0 flex justify-end"><div class="touch:-me-2 touch:-ms-3.5 -ms-2.5 -me-1 flex flex-wrap items-center gap-y-4 p-1 select-none focus-within:transition-none hover:transition-none touch:pointer-events-auto touch:opacity-100 duration-300 group-hover/turn-messages:delay-300 pointer-events-none opacity-0 motion-safe:transition-opacity group-hover/turn-messages:pointer-events-auto group-hover/turn-messages:opacity-100 group-focus-within/turn-messages:pointer-events-auto group-focus-within/turn-messages:opacity-100 has-data-[state=open]:pointer-events-auto has-data-[state=open]:opacity-100" style="mask-position: 0% 0%;"><button class="text-token-text-secondary hover:bg-token-bg-secondary rounded-lg" aria-label="Copy" aria-pressed="false" data-testid="copy-turn-action-button" data-state="closed"><span class="flex items-center justify-center touch:w-10 h-8 w-8"><svg width="20" height="20" viewBox="0 0 20 20" fill="currentColor" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" class="icon"><path d="M12.668 10.667C12.668 9.95614 12.668 9.46258 12.6367 9.0791C12.6137 8.79732 12.5758 8.60761 12.5244 8.46387L12.4688 8.33399C12.3148 8.03193 12.0803 7.77885 11.793 7.60254L11.666 7.53125C11.508 7.45087 11.2963 7.39395 10.9209 7.36328C10.5374 7.33197 10.0439 7.33203 9.33301 7.33203H6.5C5.78896 7.33203 5.29563 7.33195 4.91211 7.36328C4.63016 7.38632 4.44065 7.42413 4.29688 7.47559L4.16699 7.53125C3.86488 7.68518 3.61186 7.9196 3.43555 8.20703L3.36524 8.33399C3.28478 8.49198 3.22795 8.70352 3.19727 9.0791C3.16595 9.46259 3.16504 9.95611 3.16504 10.667V13.5C3.16504 14.211 3.16593 14.7044 3.19727 15.0879C3.22797 15.4636 3.28473 15.675 3.36524 15.833L3.43555 15.959C3.61186 16.2466 3.86474 16.4807 4.16699 16.6348L4.29688 16.6914C4.44063 16.7428 4.63025 16.7797 4.91211 16.8027C5.29563 16.8341 5.78896 16.835 6.5 16.835H9.333