<h2 data-start="1467" data-end="1485">Core Principles</h2>
<ul data-start="1487" data-end="1895">
<li data-start="1487" data-end="1552">
<p data-start="1489" data-end="1552"><strong data-start="1489" data-end="1511">Thought is sparse.</strong> Most possible ideas are never activated.</p>
</li>
<li data-start="1553" data-end="1647">
<p data-start="1555" data-end="1647"><strong data-start="1555" data-end="1581">Meaning has structure.</strong> Representations should reflect real symmetries, not correlations.</p>
</li>
<li data-start="1648" data-end="1726">
<p data-start="1650" data-end="1726"><strong data-start="1650" data-end="1673">Entropy has limits.</strong> Coherence must be bounded, conserved, or compressed.</p>
</li>
<li data-start="1727" data-end="1811">
<p data-start="1729" data-end="1811"><strong data-start="1729" data-end="1756">Alignment is geometric.</strong> Unsafe goals should be <em data-start="1780" data-end="1793">unreachable</em>, not discouraged.</p>
</li>
<li data-start="1812" data-end="1895">
<p data-start="1814" data-end="1895"><strong data-start="1814" data-end="1846">Platforms shouldn’t extract.</strong> Attention and contribution must not be zero-sum.</p>
</li>
</ul>
